<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indragiri River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indragiri River rises in the Minangkabau highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sumatra">West Sumatra</a>, where it is called the Kuantan, and flows east through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> province into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>. For centuries it carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a>, gold and forest products from the interior to the coast, and the Indragiri Sultanate grew up along it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indragiri-river.jpg" alt="Indragiri River" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isaak de Graaf · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AMH-5140-NA_Map_of_the_Rokan_and_Indragiri_rivers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
